# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/security/
# (quick task 260827-np1). Mirrors every sibling module manifest's own
# standing instruction (see modules/screensaver/qmldir, modules/lock/qmldir,
# modules/osd/qmldir): any .qml type added to this directory that is NOT
# declared below becomes unresolvable, with no load error — it simply
# reads `undefined` forever. qml-import-check enforces this. Any FUTURE
# type added here MUST be declared in the same commit that creates it.
#
# ── THE `singleton` KEYWORD IS LOAD-BEARING ───────────────────────────
# Severity and SecurityBackend each carry `pragma Singleton` AND are
# marked `singleton` below. modules/qmldir's own header records why both
# are required, binary-verified in 12-06: without the qmldir keyword, a
# bare `SecurityBackend.findings`-style access resolves to `undefined`
# forever and the object is never constructed. Removing either one is a
# silent, error-free failure.
#
# SecurityBackend is the singleton that owns every probe AND the running
# scan. It is a singleton specifically so a scan outlives the page that
# started it — see its own header for the measurement that forced this.
# The bar capsule, the dashboard tab and both settings layouts are four
# readers of ONE backend, never four backends.
module qs.modules.security

singleton Severity 1.0 Severity.qml
singleton SecurityBackend 1.0 SecurityBackend.qml

# ── Surfaces ──
SecurityOverview 1.0 SecurityOverview.qml
# ONE settings layout. Plates S1 and S2 shipped as a picker and were
# merged in operator round 3 ("both security layouts feel redundant, they
# should be combined") — SecurityOverview keeps S2's verdict header and
# ranking AND S1's domain grouping, ordering domains by their own worst
# finding. There is no `security.pageLayout` pref any more.

# Plate D1 — the dashboard drawer tab.
SecurityTab 1.0 SecurityTab.qml

# Plate H1's bar half is NOT here. Operator round 2 moved it from a
# standalone capsule to an ActionCell inside
# modules/bar/ClockActionsCapsule.qml, beside the notification bell —
# that cluster is where this bar's status glyphs live, and a lone capsule
# in endZone was both mispositioned and a second thing changing that
# zone's height. There is no SecurityCapsule.qml any more.

# Shared row primitive used by both settings layouts and the tab, so a
# finding renders identically wherever it appears.
FindingRow 1.0 FindingRow.qml
